# XCU env
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# env is reached through PATH (and by exec where it matters). The
# utilities run under it are sh -c command strings and small scripts the
# test writes in its own directory. A file without execute permission
# stands for the found-but-cannot-run case, and a name that does not exist
# stands for not found.

assertion  XCU.env.001
anchor     utilities/env.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/env.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       env with no utility writes the environment, one name=value
           line each, so an exported variable appears as its line.
test       t/001-print.sh

assertion  XCU.env.002
anchor     utilities/env.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/env.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       name=value operands are put into the environment of the utility,
           replace an inherited variable of the same name, and do not
           change the environment of the caller.
test       t/002-assign.sh

assertion  XCU.env.003
anchor     utilities/env.html#OPTIONS
class      required
since      1992
says       env -i gives the utility exactly the variables named by the
           operands and nothing inherited.
test       t/003-ignore.sh

assertion  XCU.env.004
anchor     utilities/env.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       env exits with the status of the utility it ran, 127 when the
           utility cannot be found, and 126 when it is found but cannot be
           run.
test       t/004-status.sh

assertion  XCU.env.005
anchor     utilities/env.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
anchor     utilities/env.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      1992
says       A PATH=value operand is the PATH used to find the utility.
test       t/005-path-operand.sh

assertion  XCU.env.006
anchor     utilities/env.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      1992
says       The argument operands are passed to the utility unchanged and in
           order.
test       t/006-arguments.sh

assertion  XCU.env.007
anchor     utilities/env.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       When a utility is given, env itself writes nothing to standard
           output.
test       t/007-silent.sh

assertion  XCU.env.008
anchor     utilities/env.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.4
class      required
since      1992
says       env accepts -- as the end of options, so a name=value operand
           and a utility follow it.
test       t/008-double-dash.sh

assertion  XCU.env.009
anchor     utilities/env.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      1992
says       A name=value operand with an empty value sets the variable to
           the empty string.
test       t/009-empty-value.sh
